# clangd / editor support for the firmware.
#
# No build directory is named here on purpose.  Every build directory writes its
# own compile_commands.json (CMakeLists.txt sets CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS),
# and clangd finds one by itself -- it searches the source tree and a "build"
# subdirectory -- so this file only has to stay a valid (empty) mapping.
#
# build-pico2/ is not one of clangd's default names, so CMakeLists.txt keeps a
# link named compile_commands.json at the top of the tree pointing at the build
# directory it is configuring: whatever was configured last is what the editor
# sees, so re-run cmake in the directory you want (no config to edit).
#
# See notes/build-and-flash.md ("编辑器 / clangd").
#
# The recorded commands invoke arm-none-eabi-gcc, so give clangd that compiler's
# builtin include paths as well -- start it as
#
#     clangd --query-driver=/usr/bin/arm-none-eabi-*
#
# (VS Code passes it for you, see .vscode/settings.json) if diagnostics about
# missing headers such as stdint.h show up.
CompileFlags: {}
